{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Difficult Relationships", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Man's Best Friend", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in the present, past or future in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Perfect Modals - Review", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Let's review the Perfect Modals - verbs you use to add the meaning of certainty, uncertainty, past possibility and regret.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "She's used to getting her breakfast at exactly that time every day, and she<span class=\"strong\"> would have thought</span> that this particular Friday was no exception.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">should have known </span>Coco wouldn't want to do the same.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I always think that she <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> possibly<span class=\"strong\"> have heard</span> anything, but her doggy sense is far more powerful than my human ears. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Forms\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">must have done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this is very likely what happened, but you have no way of knowing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">They didn't come to the meeting. They must have been delayed.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">may / might / could have done \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this is possibly what happened, but you have no way of knowing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm not sure why he isn't here yet. He may have been caught in traffic.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this did not happen even though everything pointed to it being possible - this form is often used to express regret\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I could have learned French when I was in Paris, but I didn't apply myself.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">should have / ought to have done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this did not happen even though it was necessary - this form is also used to express regret\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I should have known Coco wouldn't want to do the same.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this did not happen even though that was the original intention - something got in the way of that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">She's used to getting her breakfast at exactly that time every day, and she would have thought that this particular Friday was no exception.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">can't have done \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this is almost impossible to have happened\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">He can't have arrived yet. His bus was delayed.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " State Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "State Verbs are verbs that talk about a state rather than an action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Look at the chart for a summary of how and when to use these specific verbs:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Forms\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Examples\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous</span> + State Verbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the event described is transitory and happens at a past time not far from the present (look, love, sound, like, etc.)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"   <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm loving this new restaurant. We should come here more often.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous </span>+ Mental States Verbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it describes a growing awareness of something (find, think, realize, understand, etc.)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm realizing my boss is completely incompetent.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"these are verbs which perform the action they describe (advise, confess, deny, permit, suggest, refuse, thank, etc.)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I admit I made a mistake.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I confess that I have a bit of a bias, but I think they are among the most intelligent animals.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She loves having company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She instantly realized that she had made a mistake and ran off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She regretted that she had to spend an hour in her cage.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "bright", "type": "name"}, {"content": "intelligent", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: First, like humans, dogs are bright and resourceful. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words to review. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "resourceful", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having the ability to find quick and clever ways to overcome difficulties", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Dogs can be very resourceful at getting what they want. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "intuitive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having the ability to find quick and clever ways to overcome difficulties", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Second, dogs are intuitive. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "kind-hearted", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a kind and sympathetic nature", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most dogs are naturally gentle and kind-hearted.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "personable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a \u200bpleasing and \u200battractive \u200bmanner", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Third, canines are kind-hearted and personable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cheeky", "type": "name"}, {"content": " slightly \u200brude or \u200bshowing no \u200brespect, but often in a \u200bfunny way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Finally, dogs can be cheeky and disobedient.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "disobedient", "type": "name"}, {"content": "refusing to obey rules or someone in authority", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A disobedient dog may need to get some training.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le08ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Draw a Venn diagram consisting of two overlapping circles on a blank piece of paper.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Above one circle write the heading \u201cDogs\u201d. Above the other, write \u201cHumans\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In the \u201cDog\u201d circle, write all of the adjectives you can think of that describe dogs. Do the same for the \u201cHuman\u201d circle.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In the overlapping area, include all adjectives that describe both dogs and humans.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I create a Venn diagram.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write adjectives that describe dogs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write adjectives that describe humans.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I choose several adjectives that describe both dogs and humans.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn11le08ob11re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn11le08ob11re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "Let me just start by saying that I know humans and dogs are different. Really, I do. But there are a few ways in which our personality traits are actually quite similar to those of our canine friends.<br/>\nFirst, like humans, dogs are bright and resourceful. Take my dog Coco for example. Last Friday she prevented me from sleeping in by scratching on my bedroom door at 6:00 a.m. She's used to getting her breakfast at exactly that time every day, and she would have thought that this particular Friday was no exception. The problem was that it was Easter Friday, a holiday, and I was looking forward to getting a bit of extra rest. I should have known Coco wouldn't want to do the same. Eventually she got tired of waiting, went into the kitchen, opened a bag of Doritos with her paw and gobbled up the entire thing. I confess that I have a bit of a bias, but I think they are among the most intelligent animals."}, {"image": "engenn11le08ob11re2img02.jpg", "time": "59900", "id": 2, "text": "Second, dogs are intuitive. Coco always barks at least ten seconds before I hear anyone at the door. I always think that she can't possibly have heard anything, but her doggy sense is far more powerful than my human ears. <br/>\nThird, canines are kindhearted and personable. She loves having company. Just last week, my brother visited, and Coco must have brought out every single one of her toys and set them at his feet. She wanted to share her most valuable treasures with him. Of course, she also insisted on his scratching her belly in return for her generosity."}, {"image": "engenn11le08ob11re2img03.jpg", "time": "100000", "id": 3, "text": "Finally, dogs can be cheeky and disobedient. Last week, as I was eating burgers for dinner, she jumped up and grabbed one right off my plate. She instantly realized that she had made a mistake and ran off. She regretted that she had to spend an hour in her cage, surely, but for her the punishment was worth the crime."}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le08ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le08ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can express uncertainty about past events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about two actions together.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can describe a temporary situation, a mental state or the type of function of a statement. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What animals do you think make the best pets? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " If you had a dog, what tricks would you train it to do?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " Let's review!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC",